# Search technical

When these files (or equivalent metadata in a framework) are in play:

- Main content must appear in the first HTML response. Client-only text is
  not "done" for search or for agents.
- One topic, one URL. Set a canonical. Do not ship near-duplicate paths
  without a redirect or canonical plan.
- Title, meta description, and H1 describe the same page. One H1.
- Links Google should follow are real `<a href>` URLs, not JS-only clicks.
- Images and video have descriptive alt / captions when they carry meaning.
- JSON-LD is valid JSON, uses a real Schema.org type, and repeats only
  facts visible on the page. Prefer one `@graph` over contradictory blocks.
- `robots.txt` must not `Disallow: /` for `Googlebot` unless the user wants
  the site out of Google. Search/cite bots: `crawlers.md` in
  `auditing-search-visibility`.
- `llms.txt` is optional agent navigation. It does not replace robots and
  is not a Google ranking file.
- Framework metadata (Next.js `metadata`, `generateMetadata`, `sitemap.ts`)
  must emit the same facts as the rendered page. Do not set a title in
  metadata that the H1 contradicts.
